cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  FoldNTT: A Multiplier- and Twiddle-Lean NTT Core with Formally Verified
  Arithmetic for Proth Primes
message: >-
  If you use this artifact, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kamba
    given-names: Masato
    affiliation: Nyx Foundation
repository-code: 'https://github.com/NyxFoundation/FoldNTT'
abstract: >-
  FoldNTT is a redesign of the released radix-2 CFNTT accelerator (TCHES
  2022) for the Falcon / FN-DSA prime q = 12289 with one hardware multiplier
  per butterfly instead of three (shift-add K-RED reduction) and about half
  the stored twiddle constants (a psi-fold of the bit-reversed table). Every
  arithmetic and pipeline block is proven with exact-width SMT (z3) and
  compositional SymbiYosys proofs, control-safety invariants by k-induction,
  the proofs are mutation-tested, and the composed transform is validated by
  simulation, all rerun by CI. Checking the released RTL against the
  mathematics exposed an inverse-transform bug (a missing per-stage halving,
  reported upstream) that the retrofit corrects. The repository also carries a
  reconstructed controller for the reference core (its FSM was never
  released), a sequential core with its own controller that builds to a
  Basys-3 bitstream through a fully open flow (yosys + openXC7), and a
  generator that instantiates the reducer for other Proth primes (validated
  exhaustively on ML-KEM q = 3329).
keywords:
  - number-theoretic-transform
  - post-quantum-cryptography
  - formal-verification
  - FPGA
  - Falcon
  - Kyber
  - K-RED
  - SymbiYosys
license: MIT
